SUMMARY:Inside the Artist’s Studio Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:YoloArts is celebrating our county’s resident Artists and taking a unique look into their studio spaces in Gallery 625’s current exhibition “Inside the Artist’s Studio”\, which highlights the wide range of artwork being created within our community. \nBy displaying both the artists’ spaces and the artwork created therein\, we honor the labor and creative process of humanity. Moreover\, we are documenting a moment in time to gain a deeper understanding of the artistic processes of Yolo County Artists. \nFeatured Artists include Aashi Labana\, Amellia Soto\, Elyse Doyle-Martinez\, Jamie Seibel\, Jordan Benton\, June Daskalakis\, Linda Zhong\, Sandra Ledesma-Swogger\, Sandra Violet Clark\, and Tyler Rico. \nInside the Artist’s Studio is on view through October 30\, 2026. Regular open hours of Gallery 625 are Monday – Friday from 8 a.m. – 5 p.m. \nGallery 625 is located in the Erwin Meyer County Administration building at 625 Court St. in Woodland. \nArtwork: The Struggle Has Always Been Inner by Elyse Doyle-Martinez
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/inside-the-artists-studio-exhibition/
LOCATION:Gallery 625\, 625 Court St\, Erwin Meier Admin Building\, Woodland\, CA\, 95776\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art,Community
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Doyle-Martinez.jpg
END:VEVENT
